rror","title":"Lockheed Martin (LMT) Statistics & Valuation","url":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/lmt/statistics/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/ups/","image":"https://stockanalysis.com/stockanalysis-1200x630.png","text":"United Parcel Service (UPS) Stock Price & Overview\n\n# United Parcel Service, Inc. (UPS)\n\nNYSE: UPS · Real-Time Price · USD\n\n101.06 -0.46 (-0.45%) At close: Oct 23, 2026, 4:00 PM EDT\n\n101.05 -0.01 (-0.01%) After-hours: Oct 23, 2026, 7:57 PM EDT\n\n| Market Cap | 85.98B +16.5% |\n| --- | --- |\n| Revenue (ttm) | 89.93B -0.4% |\n| Net Income | 4.57B -20.2% |\n| EPS | 5.38 -20.0% |\n| Shares Out | 850.78M |\n| PE Ratio | 18.79 |\n| Forward PE | 13.00 |\n| Dividend | $6.56 (6.49%) |\n| Ex-Dividend Date | Aug 17, 2026 |\n\n| Volume | 3,603,208 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Open | 100.90 |\n| Previous Close | 101.52 |\n| Day's Range | 99.08 - 101.58 |\n| 52-Week Range | 86.30 - 122.41 |\n| Beta | 1.05 |\n| Analysts | Buy |\n| Price Target | 114.27 (+13.07%) |\n| Earnings Date | Oct 27, 2026 |\n\n## About UPS\n\nUnited Parcel Service, Inc., a package delivery and logistics provider, offers transportation and delivery services. It operates through two segments, U.S. Domestic Package and International Package. The U.S. Domestic Package segment offers time-definite delivery services for express letters, documents, packages and palletized freight through air and ground services. The International Package segment provides small package operations in Europe, the Middle East and Africa, Canada and Latin America, and Asia. The company offers a range of guarant... [Read more]\n\nIndustry Integrated Freight & Logistics\n\nSector Industrials\n\nIPO Date Nov 10, 1999\n\nEmployees 460,000\n\nStock Exchange NYSE\n\nTicker Symbol UPS\n\nWebsite https://www.ups.com\n\n## Financial Performance\n\nIn 2025, UPS's revenue was $88.66 billion, a decrease of -2.65% compared to the previous year's $91.07 billion. Earnings were $5.57 billion, a decrease of -3.63%.\n\n## Analyst Summary\n\nAccording to 29 analysts, the average rating for UPS stock is \"Buy.\" The 12-month stock price target is $114.27, which is an increase of 13.07% from the latest price.\n\nPrice Target $114.27 (13.07% upside) Analyst Consensus: Buy\n\nMounting macro pressures are what Jason Brown (@brownreport) sees hitting the stock market for the foreseeable future. That said, he points to trading opportunities in stocks he expects to weather thr...\n\n6 weeks ago - Schwab Network\n\n### UPS Rejiggers Operating Model, Names Chief Global Operations Officer\n\nThe company shook up its executive roles as part of the new model, naming the head of its U.S. business to lead its global operations, among other appointments.\n\n7 weeks ago - WSJ\n\n### UPS names Ramos Chief International, Healthcare and Supply Chain Officer\n\nUPS (UPS) announced that Kate Gutmann, Executive Vice President and President, International, Healthcare and Supply Chain Solutions, will retire for personal family reasons. Gutmann will be succeeded ...\n\n### UPS says to ‘standardize critical operational processes across geographies’\n\n### UPS Announces Executive Leadership Changes and New Global Operating Model Effective September 1, 2026\n\n### UPS and 6 More Stocks Beating 10-Year Treasuries\n\nVerizon, Altria and United Parcel Service are among the companies with dividend yields that match or beat bonds and also boast solid earnings prospects.\n\n### UPS Invests $2 Billion to Future-Proof Global Supply Chains\n\nUPS plans to invest a total of more than $2 billion into its international, healthcare and supply chain businesses between 2024 and 2028, an executive told CNBC in a report published Monday (Aug. 24).\n\n### UPS announces investments over $2B across Healthcare, Supply Chain businesses\n\n### UPS is investing $2 billion in international, healthcare and supply chain businesses","title":"United Parcel Service (UPS) Stock Price & Overview","url":"https://stockanalysis.com