finishing, document creation, design solutions, direct mail, signs and graphics, custom-branded boxes, copying, computer rental, Wi-Fi, corporate print solutions, shredding, ... [Read more]\n\nIndustry Integrated Freight & Logistics\n\nSector Industrials\n\nFounded 1971\n\nEmployees 530,000\n\nStock Exchange NYSE\n\nTicker Symbol FDX\n\nWebsite https://www.fedex.com\n\n## Financial Performance\n\nIn fiscal year 2026, FedEx's revenue was $94.72 billion, an increase of 7.73% compared to the previous year's $87.93 billion. Earnings were $4.43 billion, an increase of 8.29%.\n\n## Analyst Summary\n\nAccording to 28 analysts, the average rating for FDX stock is \"Buy.\" The 12-month stock price target is $356.27, which is an increase of 19.27% from the latest price.\n\nPrice Target $356.27 (19.27% upside) Analyst Consensus: Buy\n\n### The Big 3: FDX, HD, QCOM\n\n### ‘The Fuel for AI' at FedEx\n\nFedEx CEO Raj Subramaniam is my guest on this week's episode of WSJ Leadership Institute Presents: Leaders. And while Subramaniam may not be as well-known as his iconic predecessor Fred Smith, he has ...\n\n4 weeks ago - WSJ\n\n### FedEx, Advent-led consortium secures over 89% of InPost shares in takeover offer\n\nPolish parcel locker operator InPost said on ​Friday that 89.81% of its shares ‌had been tendered in the offer from a consortium made up of FedEx , ​Advent International and other InPost ​investors.\n\n5 weeks ago - Reuters\n\n### IWP Capital to vote ‘FOR’ FedEx Proposal 6 on abortion-drug distribution risk\n\nIWP Capital, a faith-based service provider and co-filer of Proposal 6 on the FedEx (FDX) 2026 proxy statement, said it intends to vote FOR the proposal at the company’s annual…\n\n### IWP Capital to Vote \"FOR\" FedEx Proposal 6 on Abortion-Drug Distribution Risk\n\n### FedEx Launches FedEx Authenticated Delivery for Added Security on High-Value and Sensitive Shipments\n\nMEMPHIS, Tenn.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--FedEx Corp. (NYSE: FDX) today announced the launch of FedEx® Authenticated Delivery, a new premium delivery option that provides greater confidence for select shipment...\n\n### FedEx expands sustainable aviation fuel agreements across U.S. air network\n\n### FedEx Introduces Global Trade Navigator to Simplify International Shipping\n\n### FedEx Transcript: Citi’s 2026 Global TMT Conference\n\nManagement outlined progress toward $6B free cash flow and double-digit earnings growth by 2029, driven by cost reduction, network integration, and technology. AI and data initiatives are enhancing efficiency, enabling new services, and expanding into high-value verticals and government contracts.\n\n### FedEx price target lowered to $400 from $460 at JPMorgan","title":"FedEx (FDX) Stock Price & Overview","url":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/fdx/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/fdx/statistics/","image":"https://stockanalysis.com/stockanalysis-1200x630.png","text":"FedEx (FDX) Statistics & Valuation\n\n298.72 -5.20 (-1.71%) At close: Oct 23, 2026, 4:00 PM EDT\n\n298.99 +0.27 (0.09%) After-hours: Oct 23, 2026, 7:57 PM EDT\n\n## Total Valuation\n\nFedEx has a market cap or net worth of $70.70 billion. The enterprise value is $100.09 billion.\n\n| Market Cap | 70.70B |\n| --- | --- |\n| Enterprise Value | 100.09B |\n\n## Important Dates\n\nThe next confirmed earnings date is Wednesday, October 28, 2026, after market close.\n\n| Earnings Date | Oct 28, 2026 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ex-Dividend Date | Sep 14, 2026 |\n\n## Share Statistics\n\nFedEx has 236.67 million shares outstanding. The number of shares has decreased by -1.65% in one year.\n\n| Current Share Class | 236.67M |\n| --- | --- |\n| Shares Outstanding | 236.67M |\n| Shares Change (YoY) | -1.65% |\n| Shares Change (QoQ) | +0.84% |\n| Owned by Insiders (%) | 0.26% |\n| Owned by Institutions (%) | 82.90% |\n| Float | 218.66M |\n\n## Valuation Ratios\n\nThe trailing PE ratio is 16.10 and the forward PE ratio is 15.65. FedEx's PEG ratio is 1.42.\n\n| PE Ratio |